// A hand-written entry point for a generated class. `@PROG@` is the name of
// that class; substitute it (the harness does, in test/stages/java.sh).
//
// The compiler generates no `main`: a generated class only exposes
// `public static Object body()`, the program's value, so it can be used as a
// library. This file is the entry point the test harness uses.
//
// It goes through `Rt.runMain` rather than printing `body()` directly: that
// evaluates and prints the body on a thread with a large stack (generated
// recursion is mostly non-tail) and turns an exception into a non-zero exit
// status. The body is passed as an `Rt.Fn` so it runs on that thread; the
// argument is ignored.
//
// Compile all three together:
//   javac -d <dir> <dir>/Rt.java <dir>/@PROG@.java <dir>/Main.java
//   java -cp <dir> Main
public final class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Rt.runMain(new Rt.Fn() {
      public Object apply(Object ignored) {
        return @PROG@.body();
      }
    });
  }
}
